# vitabrowser: ship a near-empty monkey user.css
#
# The MacSurf content core's lifecycle (fixes551) treats a FAILED fetch of the
# user stylesheet as a fatal content error. Pristine NetSurf ships no
# frontends/monkey/res/user.css, so resource:user.css 404s and the patched
# engine loops: fetch -> LIFE UNACCEPT -> NAV ERROR 24 -> error page ->
# re-discover stylesheets -> re-fetch. A comment-only user.css keeps the fetch
# successful with zero styling effect.
#
# New file:
#   frontends/monkey/res/user.css
#
# Applies to: netsurf (after the generated stack)
--- /dev/null	2026-09-22 08:45:00.000000000 +0100
+++ b/frontends/monkey/res/user.css	2026-09-22 08:45:00.000000000 +0100
@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@
+/* user.css — user stylesheet (MacSurf/VitaBrowser)
+ *
+ * The MacSurf content core's lifecycle treats a failed fetch of the
+ * user stylesheet as a fatal content error (fixes551). Pristine NetSurf
+ * ships no user.css, so the resource: fetch 404s and the patched engine
+ * loops on the error page. Shipping a near-empty user.css keeps the
+ * fetch successful with zero styling effect.
+ */
